+/* CI3 lays its forms out on a bootstrap col-lg-6 grid: two field columns, each label sitting
+   directly above its control. Opting a form in with .form-grid gives the same shape; the grid
+   only works on forms whose label/control pairs are wrapped in .field, so the class is added
+   per form rather than to `form` globally. Anything that spans the full width (fieldsets of
+   checkboxes, the button row) says so explicitly. */
+.form-grid {
+    display: grid;
+    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
